00:44:54.180 --> 00:44:59.040
And many times that I filmed there with Rain, one time I took my camera and I took

1015
00:44:59.040 --> 00:45:02.960
all of these kind of artsy photos and I took an artsy photo of the mailbox.

1016
00:45:04.880 --> 00:45:05.940
But I love it.

1017
00:45:06.100 --> 00:45:07.600
I actually think it'd be really cool.

1018
00:45:07.740 --> 00:45:09.860
Like I should like blow it up like canvas size.

1019
00:45:10.000 --> 00:45:10.860
I think it looks really cool.

1020
00:45:11.060 --> 00:45:17.020
We had a fan question about this scene of Jim and Pam arriving at Shroot Farms from Amaya

1021
00:45:17.020 --> 00:45:17.580
Norsey.

1022
00:45:18.200 --> 00:45:24.440
She said at around eight minutes, 21 seconds, Moe's appears behind their car and starts running

1023
00:45:24.440 --> 00:45:25.400
alongside them.

1024
00:45:25.620 --> 00:45:27.180
How was that decided?

1025
00:45:27.180 --> 00:45:30.580
Because it's really funny and it creates Moe's personality.

1026
00:45:30.900 --> 00:45:32.320
I reached out to Paul.

1027
00:45:32.500 --> 00:45:33.960
I would love to hear what he says.

1028
00:45:34.440 --> 00:45:42.040
Well, first of all, he came up with the idea for Moe's running alongside the car while in

1029
00:45:42.040 --> 00:45:43.100
a cafe in Russia.

1030
00:45:44.480 --> 00:45:47.980
I love how it's like his inspiration is in Russia.

1031
00:45:48.240 --> 00:45:48.620
It's hilarious.

1032
00:45:48.980 --> 00:45:54.920
I love how he's always in these like foreign countries when he is writing these scripts and

1033
00:45:54.920 --> 00:45:55.920
having his good ideas.

1034
00:45:55.940 --> 00:46:02.380
But he said he started laughing out loud at the idea of Moe's running alongside the car,

1035
00:46:02.600 --> 00:46:03.800
quote, like a dog.

1036
00:46:04.520 --> 00:46:06.400
And that's what he wrote in the script.

1037
00:46:06.400 --> 00:46:12.460
So that moment was totally scripted that Moe's would run alongside the car like a puppy dog

1038
00:46:12.460 --> 00:46:14.280
to greet the new visitors.

1039
00:46:14.620 --> 00:46:20.460
And it was written by an American tourist in Russia laughing out loud by himself to no one.

1040
00:46:20.780 --> 00:46:21.720
In a cafe.

1041
00:46:22.380 --> 00:46:27.080
Well, I wanted to commend Mike Schur on how fast he is.

1042
00:46:27.260 --> 00:46:28.380
I was like, dang.

1043
00:46:30.000 --> 00:46:33.440
And you guys, we filmed that several times.

1044
00:46:33.440 --> 00:46:38.740
We filmed that arrival because we had to film it with a cameraman inside the car.

1045
00:46:38.880 --> 00:46:43.660
But then we also have a shot of us driving where we took the cameraman out of the car

1046
00:46:43.660 --> 00:46:46.000
and they just shot John and I.

1047
00:46:46.220 --> 00:46:49.440
So, I mean, Mike ran a lot that day.

1048
00:46:50.100 --> 00:46:52.620
Well, I think Mike was put through the ringer in this episode.

1049
00:46:52.860 --> 00:46:59.760
There is a whole deleted scene where he is jumping on a kind of busted trampoline for Pam and Jim

1050
00:46:59.760 --> 00:47:01.300
and doing all of these things.

1051
00:47:01.300 --> 00:47:02.820
Helicopter, look over here.

1052
00:47:02.960 --> 00:47:04.120
And he's doing like constantly.

1053
00:47:04.320 --> 00:47:07.180
He was on that trampoline doing tons of stuff.

1054
00:47:07.960 --> 00:47:10.580
He must have been so sore after this day.

1055
00:47:10.900 --> 00:47:11.880
And hot and tired.

1056
00:47:12.320 --> 00:47:12.640
Yeah.

1057
00:47:13.520 --> 00:47:15.280
Well, lady, why don't we take a break?

1058
00:47:15.440 --> 00:47:19.760
And when we come back, we're going to meet Nick Figaro, manager to the stars,

1059
00:47:20.300 --> 00:47:24.040
and also take a look inside Shrook FarMs.

1060
00:47:24.320 --> 00:47:25.200
I like it.

1061
00:47:25.880 --> 00:47:26.400
All right.

1062
00:47:26.500 --> 00:47:28.900
I'm going to take a break and I will not be on a yacht,

1063
00:47:28.920 --> 00:47:30.520
but I might be doing some magic.

1064
00:47:40.740 --> 00:47:41.760
So now we are back.

1065
00:47:42.000 --> 00:47:47.540
Michael is in his cubicle at the telemarketing company and his boss, Nick Figaro, notices the

1066
00:47:47.540 --> 00:47:48.100
camera crew.

1067
00:47:48.260 --> 00:47:49.100
He walks over.

1068
00:47:49.260 --> 00:47:50.340
He's like, what's happening here?

1069
00:47:50.580 --> 00:47:51.580
Michael's like, it's okay.

1070
00:47:51.760 --> 00:47:52.400
They're with me.

1071
00:47:52.540 --> 00:47:56.520
And then he has this very funny speech where he's like, we're a legitimate operation.

1072
00:47:57.020 --> 00:47:58.700
Like, clearly they're not.

1073
00:47:59.000 --> 00:47:59.980
Because he's clearly not.

1074
00:48:00.260 --> 00:48:01.700
He has to like point that out.

1075
00:48:02.420 --> 00:48:07.060
Well, the actor who plays Nick Figaro is Alan Wasserman.

1076
00:48:07.620 --> 00:48:09.600
And here are some other roles that he has played.

1077
00:48:09.700 --> 00:48:13.740
He's done a ton of television shows, but I also found it interesting that he played the

1078
00:48:13.740 --> 00:48:20.440
gym teacher in the Tom Hanks movie Big and the job interviewer in the Tom Cruise movie Cocktails.

1079
00:48:20.440 --> 00:48:22.060
Oh, wow.

1080
00:48:22.880 --> 00:48:25.460
Oh, those are two great movies.

1081
00:48:26.400 --> 00:48:31.700
Well, my favorite thing is when he does what Michael always does.

1082
00:48:31.880 --> 00:48:33.440
He calls a conference room meeting.

1083
00:48:33.760 --> 00:48:34.780
Five minutes.

1084
00:48:35.220 --> 00:48:37.240
And Michael's like, oh, these things are useless.

1085
00:48:37.780 --> 00:48:38.320
Yes.

1086
00:48:38.320 --> 00:48:43.440
And then in this conference room meeting, when Nick Figaro is trying to explain how to

1087
00:48:43.440 --> 00:48:47.040
make a sale, Michael is just making jokes under his breath.

1088
00:48:47.900 --> 00:48:48.420
Yes.

1089
00:48:48.580 --> 00:48:51.340
And his co-workers love him.

1090
00:48:51.900 --> 00:48:54.420
He's the gem of the telemarketing office.

1091
00:48:54.760 --> 00:48:55.560
He is.

1092
00:48:55.680 --> 00:48:57.760
And they just want him to hang out with him.

1093
00:48:57.900 --> 00:49:00.200
They're constantly inviting him to go hang out.

1094
00:49:00.420 --> 00:49:04.680
There's deleted scenes where they are just, they hang on his every word.

1095
00:49:06.020 --> 00:49:12.580
Well, I got very interested in this scene at 10 minutes, 25 seconds.

1096
00:49:13.000 --> 00:49:14.220
There is a couple.

1097
00:49:14.460 --> 00:49:15.440
Did you see them?

1098
00:49:15.720 --> 00:49:17.920
The woman is pregnant, very pregnant.

1099
00:49:18.360 --> 00:49:21.520
And this man, they're all over each other.

1100
00:49:21.700 --> 00:49:23.440
Very lovey-dovey, right?

1101
00:49:23.740 --> 00:49:26.660
And they are in all the other deleted scenes, too.

1102
00:49:26.780 --> 00:49:28.940
They're always sort of like in some kind of embrace.

1103
00:49:30.260 --> 00:49:32.540
I became a little bit obsessed with them.

1104
00:49:32.540 --> 00:49:34.740
I was like, is this woman really pregnant?

1105
00:49:35.100 --> 00:49:36.360
Were they hired as a couple?

1106
00:49:36.620 --> 00:49:37.940
What is the story here?

1107
00:49:39.360 --> 00:49:41.380
So I did a bit of a deep dive.

1108
00:49:41.600 --> 00:49:42.040
Okay.

1109
00:49:42.240 --> 00:49:45.680
I found out that the woman is an actress named Ann Maddox.

1110
00:49:46.400 --> 00:49:51.620
And then I found out that Ann Maddox is our producer, Cody's friend.

1111
00:49:52.460 --> 00:49:52.940
What?

1112
00:49:53.300 --> 00:49:54.860
They're friends on Instagram.

1113
00:49:54.860 --> 00:49:55.940
I deep dived.

1114
00:49:56.080 --> 00:49:59.000
I was like, how can I get an in with this woman, Ann?

1115
00:49:59.000 --> 00:50:02.820
So Cody reached out to her friend, and she answered all my questions.

1116
00:50:03.180 --> 00:50:05.080
Oh, give me all of it.

1117
00:50:05.140 --> 00:50:05.720
I want it.

1118
00:50:05.940 --> 00:50:06.440
Give it to me.

1119
00:50:06.860 --> 00:50:07.160
Okay.

1120
00:50:07.400 --> 00:50:08.640
Here's how it went down.

1121
00:50:09.200 --> 00:50:14.240
Ann was a performer at UCB, and she said that there was a request for female performers

1122
00:50:14.240 --> 00:50:16.040
to come in for a role on The Office.

1123
00:50:16.620 --> 00:50:22.720
She was not pregnant in real life, but the role was for a young pregnant woman working nights

1124
00:50:22.720 --> 00:50:29.340
alongside her baby daddy, and it was scripted that this couple would be lovey-dovey and affectionate

1125
00:50:29.340 --> 00:50:29.920
constantly.

1126
00:50:30.260 --> 00:50:35.700
So she auditioned, she got the role, and then she got paired with this other actor randomly.

1127
00:50:36.400 --> 00:50:37.940
But here's what she said.

1128
00:50:38.100 --> 00:50:43.980
She said, I remember that one of the cameramen did not know that the cuddling was in the script.

1129
00:50:44.420 --> 00:50:48.600
And he kept saying to me and my co-star, you guys are so affectionate.

1130
00:50:48.600 --> 00:50:53.540
And then he turned to the other camera operator and said, they've been like this all day.

1131
00:50:53.540 --> 00:50:54.400
It's so funny.

1132
00:50:55.460 --> 00:50:57.780
And she was like, no, it was scripted.

1133
00:50:57.840 --> 00:50:58.740
It was scripted.

1134
00:51:00.540 --> 00:51:04.180
She also remembered that they shot in the LA Times building.

1135
00:51:04.560 --> 00:51:09.520
She remembered that we had amazing food and that the cast and crew were so nice.

1136
00:51:09.540 --> 00:51:15.540
But she said what's so heartwarming to her about that memory is just how everyone on set

1137
00:51:15.540 --> 00:51:17.280
treated her like a friend.

1138
00:51:17.280 --> 00:51:22.160
And the crew, the cast, she said she just had the best time of her life and she'll cherish

1139
00:51:22.160 --> 00:51:23.320
the experience forever.

1140
00:51:23.400 --> 00:51:24.700
It was so nice.

1141
00:51:24.920 --> 00:51:25.640
I love that.

1142
00:51:25.740 --> 00:51:29.660
I also love what a very specific thing that Paul did.

1143
00:51:30.000 --> 00:51:35.300
Paul was so thoughtful in filling out the world at the telemarketing company that he wrote

1144
00:51:35.300 --> 00:51:39.020
in the script that there would be a young pregnant woman and her baby daddy.

1145
00:51:39.200 --> 00:51:41.020
And that was so specific.

1146
00:51:41.020 --> 00:51:48.160
Yeah, I love that we often did that on the show where even minor characters who show up

1147
00:51:48.160 --> 00:51:50.300
for just one episode, they have a story.

1148
00:51:50.560 --> 00:51:51.440
That's so great.

1149
00:51:51.440 --> 00:51:52.700
I just love it.

1150
00:51:52.980 --> 00:51:53.220
Yeah.

1151
00:51:53.780 --> 00:51:55.900
And there were a lot of deleted scenes.

1152
00:51:56.160 --> 00:52:00.960
There's a lot of scenes you don't see of this couple and of all these people interacting

1153
00:52:00.960 --> 00:52:01.560
with Michael.

1154
00:52:01.900 --> 00:52:03.380
Yes, this couple loved Michael.

1155
00:52:03.500 --> 00:52:04.700
They invited him out to dinner.

1156
00:52:04.900 --> 00:52:06.320
There's a deleted scene with it.

1157
00:52:06.320 --> 00:52:10.160
And once again, Jenna, I feel like our set decorators were having fun because there's

1158
00:52:10.160 --> 00:52:12.120
all of these cartoon clippings.

1159
00:52:12.380 --> 00:52:13.060
So many.

1160
00:52:13.320 --> 00:52:13.780
So many.

1161
00:52:13.960 --> 00:52:21.620
And then there's a white piece of paper that says, constant, continuous Roger demands.

1162
00:52:22.240 --> 00:52:22.900
Don't know.

1163
00:52:23.260 --> 00:52:23.860
Don't know.

1164
00:52:24.220 --> 00:52:25.060
Very strange.

1165
00:52:25.220 --> 00:52:25.820
I saw it too.

1166
00:52:25.940 --> 00:52:27.020
I don't know what it means.

1167
00:52:27.280 --> 00:52:30.260
Well, Alan Wasserman as Nick Figueroa was fantastic.

1168
00:52:30.260 --> 00:52:31.520
I thought he was perfect.

1169
00:52:31.880 --> 00:52:35.700
I loved his whole, make the call, say the lines, make the sale.

1170
00:52:35.700 --> 00:52:40.720
He was just like, I believed him 100% that he was this guy.

1171
00:52:41.360 --> 00:52:48.560
Well, you know, Ange, in addition to being a silent magician, I also worked as a telemarketer.

1172
00:52:49.720 --> 00:52:54.460
And I can tell you that Alan Wasserman's performance is right on.

1173
00:52:55.460 --> 00:52:58.780
He's like every boss I ever had in my telemarketing days.

1174
00:52:59.000 --> 00:53:04.020
Well, you know, I worked at 1-800-DENTIST as an operator, and I would constantly get in

1175
00:53:04.020 --> 00:53:06.740
trouble for not saying line number 13 correctly.

1176
00:53:07.440 --> 00:53:08.220
Oh, yeah.

1177
00:53:08.380 --> 00:53:10.560
The scripts are very specific.

1178
00:53:10.920 --> 00:53:12.120
Like, they've been researched.

1179
00:53:12.120 --> 00:53:14.240
They've been put through focus groups.

1180
00:53:14.760 --> 00:53:21.240
My job was to call people and get them to subscribe to the St. Louis Post-Dispatch newspaper.

1181
00:53:21.900 --> 00:53:27.340
And we had a big deal on the Sunday paper, and I was supposed to push the Sunday paper.

1182
00:53:28.420 --> 00:53:32.680
Well, line 13, if I remember, was something about, like, you would say what their ailment

1183
00:53:32.680 --> 00:53:35.420
was and tell them the dentist you were going to send them to.

1184
00:53:36.140 --> 00:53:37.660
And it was so stilted.

1185
00:53:37.660 --> 00:53:39.960
And I remember I would say, like, you know what?

1186
00:53:40.300 --> 00:53:42.540
It sounds like, to me, you might need a root canal.

1187
00:53:42.780 --> 00:53:45.400
I mean, that kind of pain like that sounds like an abscess.

1188
00:53:45.560 --> 00:53:50.380
And literally, my manager would come in, waving his arms, and he'd be like, you are not a dental

1189
00:53:50.380 --> 00:53:51.000
professional.

1190
00:53:51.520 --> 00:53:53.180
You cannot diagnose.

1191
00:53:53.800 --> 00:53:56.180
You have to say this line exactly.

1192
00:53:56.520 --> 00:54:01.680
Well, let me help you with that toothache by finding a dentist for you in your area.

1193
00:54:01.940 --> 00:54:04.980
Like, I can't say, sounds like a root canal to me.

1194
00:54:05.260 --> 00:54:05.980
You can't.

1195
00:54:06.060 --> 00:54:07.220
What are you doing, lady?

1196
00:54:07.420 --> 00:54:08.780
So, I would get in trouble.

1197
00:54:09.000 --> 00:54:10.860
Well, Jenna, should we get to Shroop Farms?

1198
00:54:11.180 --> 00:54:12.880
Let's go to Shroop FarMs.

1199
00:54:13.280 --> 00:54:21.120
Jim and Pam are sitting on a couch in what looks like a sort of reception slash lobby area.

1200
00:54:21.120 --> 00:54:25.460
And Dwight is explaining that there are three types of rooms available.

1201
00:54:25.680 --> 00:54:26.480
He's checking them in.

1202
00:54:26.780 --> 00:54:32.020
They can stay in America, irrigation, or nighttime.

1203
00:54:33.540 --> 00:54:35.540
Pam immediately says irrigation.

1204
00:54:35.940 --> 00:54:36.800
I mean, without thought.

1205
00:54:37.020 --> 00:54:38.260
She was so positive.

1206
00:54:38.780 --> 00:54:39.000
Yeah.

1207
00:54:39.340 --> 00:54:43.900
I'm curious about nighttime, but I think I would have also chosen irrigation.

1208
00:54:44.280 --> 00:54:46.500
And by the way, it doesn't disappoint.

1209
00:54:46.500 --> 00:54:54.880
When Dwight shows them to their room, the irrigation room has a lot of pipes hanging from the walls.

1210
00:54:55.180 --> 00:54:56.540
It's a wonderful design.

1211
00:54:56.760 --> 00:54:58.360
Pipes with no purpose, though.

1212
00:54:58.940 --> 00:54:59.380
No, no, no.

1213
00:54:59.540 --> 00:55:00.360
It's decor.

1214
00:55:01.160 --> 00:55:01.280
Yeah.

1215
00:55:01.740 --> 00:55:02.620
Decorative pipes.

1216
00:55:02.940 --> 00:55:03.500
Yes.

1217
00:55:04.360 --> 00:55:06.380
And two twin beds.

1218
00:55:06.800 --> 00:55:07.100
Mm-hmm.

1219
00:55:07.640 --> 00:55:08.040
Yeah.

1220
00:55:09.020 --> 00:55:19.080
Now, I believe, I don't know if there's a deleted scene of it, but there was a scene that we shot where you see that Jim and Pam have pushed the two beds together.

1221
00:55:19.120 --> 00:55:26.980
In the morning, you see into the room, and Jim and Pam have actually made it one bed.

1222
00:55:27.400 --> 00:55:27.860
Yes.

1223
00:55:28.000 --> 00:55:30.200
And I was like, wait, is there two beds or one bed?

1224
00:55:30.300 --> 00:55:31.920
And then I realized what they had done.

1225
00:55:32.080 --> 00:55:32.360
Yes.

1226
00:55:32.360 --> 00:55:32.680
Yes.

1227
00:55:34.060 --> 00:55:40.240
But I really like this moment on the two beds with Jim and Pam when Jim says one and six.

1228
00:55:41.240 --> 00:55:42.680
And Pam's like, what?

1229
00:55:43.140 --> 00:55:44.700
And he's like, oh, I'm sorry.

1230
00:55:44.700 --> 00:55:47.560
I thought you asked me what are our chances of being murdered tonight.

1231
00:55:49.360 --> 00:55:49.880
Yeah.

1232
00:55:50.180 --> 00:55:58.160
And Jim has this really sweet talking head where he says he had this whole vision of what it would be like to have a weekend away with Pam.

1233
00:55:58.160 --> 00:56:00.420
What our first trip away would be like.

1234
00:56:00.520 --> 00:56:02.820
It's so romantic, really, and sweet.

1235
00:56:03.180 --> 00:56:07.760
And he said it definitely would not have been, you know, wine made out of beets.

1236
00:56:07.940 --> 00:56:09.240
Probably not with Dwight.

1237
00:56:09.400 --> 00:56:11.500
And definitely not with so much manure.

1238
00:56:12.300 --> 00:56:12.820
Yeah.

1239
00:56:12.900 --> 00:56:13.880
Maybe some manure.

1240
00:56:15.000 --> 00:56:16.040
But less.

1241
00:56:16.340 --> 00:56:17.000
Less manure.

1242
00:56:18.800 --> 00:56:19.320
Yeah.

1243
00:56:19.500 --> 00:56:23.900
And we filmed all of these little moments that went under this talking head.

1244
00:56:23.900 --> 00:56:28.420
So you see Dwight mashing up beets to make beet wine.

1245
00:56:28.420 --> 00:56:31.780
And then you see us out in the field helping to shovel this manure.

1246
00:56:32.140 --> 00:56:39.080
And then Moe's gets into a manure, like a snowball fight with Dwight, but he's throwing manure.

1247
00:56:39.840 --> 00:56:41.940
And I remember shooting all of that.

1248
00:56:42.120 --> 00:56:44.440
We had a fan question from Matthew K.

1249
00:56:44.960 --> 00:56:48.040
When Dwight and Pam are shoveling manure, was it real?

1250
00:56:48.800 --> 00:56:55.300
And was the moment when Moe starts throwing manure at Dwight scripted, or was that just Mike Schur messing with rain?

1251
00:56:55.980 --> 00:56:56.500
Okay.

1252
00:56:56.520 --> 00:56:57.740
It was not real manure.

1253
00:56:58.320 --> 00:56:58.760
Right.

1254
00:56:59.080 --> 00:56:59.760
It was not.

1255
00:56:59.860 --> 00:57:00.660
Of course not.

1256
00:57:00.860 --> 00:57:00.980
